PROBLEM:
Baltimore "The Charm City" is known for many good things and "Not soo good" things at the same time.
The great history of this beautiful city has some problems, just like any modern city has. 

"Taffic Congestion"

Every day, thousands of records are generated from traffic incidents, public transit systems, 
emergency services, weather conditions, demographics, and city infrastructure. Although this data exists, 
it is often spread across different systems, making it difficult to uncover meaningful 
relationships between them.

GeoVision Maryland aims to bridge that gap.

The goal is to build a Location Intelligence platform that combines GIS, analytics, 
and interactive visualization to transform raw geographic data into actionable insights. 
Rather than simply displaying maps, the platform is designed to answer practical questions that 
help governments, businesses, and communities make better decisions.

The first focus area of the project is transportation and mobility, 
beginning with traffic congestion, accident hotspots, and accessibility across 
Baltimore before expanding into broader urban intelligence use cases.